# Example requests (VS Code REST Client, Visual Studio or Rider HTTP client).
@api = http://localhost:5080

### All products
GET {{api}}/api/products

### Search + category group + sort
GET {{api}}/api/products?search=jacket&category=clothing&sort=price-asc

### Price range
GET {{api}}/api/products?minPrice=10&maxPrice=60&sort=rating

### One product
GET {{api}}/api/products/5

### Unknown product -> 404
GET {{api}}/api/products/999

### Normalised categories
GET {{api}}/api/categories

### Pricing rules used by the cart
GET {{api}}/api/store/config

### Successful simulated checkout
POST {{api}}/api/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Ada Lovelace", "email": "ada@example.com" },
  "items": [
    { "productId": 2, "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": 19, "quantity": 1 }
  ],
  "expectedTotal": 56.75
}

### Stale total -> 409 with a fresh quote
POST {{api}}/api/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Ada Lovelace", "email": "ada@example.com" },
  "items": [ { "productId": 2, "quantity": 1 } ],
  "expectedTotal": 1.00
}

### Invalid request -> 400 with field errors
POST {{api}}/api/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "A", "email": "not-an-email" },
  "items": [ { "productId": 2, "quantity": 0 } ]
}
